## Secrets

With automatic replication, Secret Manager replicates the secret across multiple regions globally, and the locations in a replication policy can't be updated after creation. So all 23 secrets must be recreated.

| | A. Recreate under the same names with `me-central2` replication | B. Regional secrets in `me-central2`, created side by side | C. Ask compliance to accept the current setup |
|---|---|---|---|
| Downtime | ⚠️ short gap per secret between delete and create; an instance restart in that gap fails | none, if the app can read regional secrets | none |
| Complexity | medium (23 secrets, values handled locally) | medium-high (possible app config change) | low |
| Reversible | no, once deleted | yes | n/a |

